// ⛔ GATED / ASPIRATIONAL EXAMPLE — does not build yet.
// The app/server layer needs language work not yet landed: async server
// components (`fn … -> @Component<ElementBase, Element>` with `use` and `await`),
// the host-bound `request()`/router, and an Element attribute model. Kept as the
// intended app-layer surface; the functional examples are jhonstart-counter /
// jhonstart-todo / jhonstart-markup.
//
// jhonstart-app — server-side rendering entry.
//
// File-based routing is a jhonstart convention (V1); here the dynamic post route
// is wired manually. `Page` is a server component (`fn -> @Component<ElementBase, Element>`):
// `await Page()` runs its loader, `renderToString` serializes the resulting
// `Element` tree to an HTML string. `main` returns `@Task<void>` so it may `await`
// (the return is the effect, botopink decision 118); `renderToString` is synchronous.

import { renderToString } from "jhonstart";
import { Page } from "jhonstart-app/app/posts/[id]/page";

fn main() -> @Task<void> {
    val html = renderToString(await Page());
    @print(html);
}
